cff-version: 1.1.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "TCM Symptom Ontology (TCM-SO): a large-scale bilingual ontology of Traditional Chinese Medicine symptoms with HPO / SNOMED CT / ICD-11 alignment"
abstract: >-
  A large-scale, bilingual (Chinese/English) OWL 2 ontology of Traditional Chinese
  Medicine (TCM) symptoms. Release v4.10 contains 1,943 classes (1,758 symptom
  classes in 31 clinical categories) with 18,046 subclass axioms and 15,790
  existential restrictions, bilingual labels on 100% of classes, and English
  textual definitions for 93.1% of symptom classes (50.4% manually translated).
  Ten system-level equivalence axioms, a symptom-level composite-definition pilot
  (9 classes), and one property chain provide GO-style faceted classification;
  an etiology layer adds 3,877 dueTo restrictions (six evils plus phlegm,
  static blood and worms). Cross-terminology alignment, confirmed by TCM domain
  experts, covers 649 HPO, 707 SNOMED CT and 973 ICD-11 mappings; 979 of 1,758
  symptom classes (55.7%) align to at least one external terminology. Logical
  consistency verified with HermiT (0 unsatisfiable classes).
